# D4: the TIMED arm with the quad ON. c2-packed-tp4-speed-quad is c2-packed-tp4-speed (the verify's T1 and T2 audits OFF, the drafter's
# K/V slide ON) with QWEN_FAST_QUAD_DRAFT=1 and NO draft audit. The same tests as D1 (warmup, coding, concurrent4, concurrent4_steady).
# The live-4 round of four steady users, the single-user coding rate and the concurrent per-user rates are read from THIS arm. The
# tokens are held against D3's (the audited arm) by the texts. The speed window's K2 (audits off, four users of which two in the ramp:
# every user drafted singly) measured a live-4 round of 170 ms: verify 63.3, four serial commits 37.9, early draft 63.8 (four
# single-user draft passes back to back on the device, about 10-11 ms each, and four serial propose calls of about 3 ms), gap 5.
# Projection to confirm or refute (four steady users, verify fixed): D5's pairs about 141 ms, D4's quad about 134 ms (the draft cut
# from 64 ms to about 26-30 ms: one 64-row pass of about 17-21 ms of device time, one collect and one batched select), i.e. per-user
# rates of 30 / 31 tok/s at 4.2 tokens per round and 71 / 75 at 10. The commits (38 ms) are not touched by this window: the four-card
# fused commit is the next lever.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card batched-draft window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/draft and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image D0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 5-15 min (the kernels are cached by D1); tests 10-15 min: 15 / 30 / 70 min.
# Read: [PACKED-PHASE] (verify: input, trace, sync, readback; commits; early draft; gap) and [PHASE] early_draft, prepare_proposals and
# propose, medians at 4 live: the round wall, early_draft (expect 26-30 ms, not 64), propose (about 0.4 ms for all four users, not 13.5),
# prepare_proposals; '[QUAD-DRAFT] round=N built=B ms=X' (the host time to enqueue the quad, built=0 rounds); the concurrent4_steady
# per-user decode_tok_s and the [ACCEPT] mean; the coding decode_tok_s. Compare with D5 (pairs) and with the speed window's K2 (singles).
# SOFT: the numbers are the product. The smoke step ENFORCES the stop conditions: an errored or empty stream, garbage text, an audit
# mismatch line, and that the quad engaged once and served at least one round with no fallback and no disable line.
# CAUTION: a busy host skews every host phase (the speed window's K2 host phases ran 10-20% slower than K1's while CI built on the rig,
# and its single-user rate read 27.5 against 35.9): check the load average around the run and repeat before believing a small gap.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-draft-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-quad
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady
